# A workspace keeps its own state in its `.troika/` directory, which is not here — this
# repo is the tree, not a workspace. The entry covers the one case where they coincide:
# running /tr:setup in this clone to dogfood it.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so it cannot match anything nested. Inside a real
# workspace the resolver writes `.troika/.gitignore` instead, which keeps the three state
# directories out of that workspace's history while committing settings and profile.
#
# WARNING: `git clean -xfd` removes it whole — uncommitted dev branches, plans, proofs,
# memory. Use explicit paths instead.
/.troika/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# Docs build and release artefacts
site/
.venv/
*.tar.gz
*.tar.gz.sha256
.cache/
